    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Parthian Empire was an Iranian power founded by the Arsacids that ruled from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#euphrates">Euphrates</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#iranian-plateau">Iranian plateau</a>.</li><li>Its cavalry held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rome">Rome</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#euphrates">Euphrates</a> for centuries, and it profited as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#silk-road">Silk Road</a> link between Rome and Han <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#china">China</a>.</li><li>Noble rivalry, civil wars and Roman captures of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ctesiphon">Ctesiphon</a> weakened it; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ardashir-i">Ardashir I</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a> ended Arsacid rule in 224 CE.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-carrhae">Carrhae</a> in 53 BCE, the Parthian general Surena kept his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#horse-archer">horse archers</a> supplied from a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#camel">camel</a> train of arrows, destroying a Roman army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#marcus-licinius-crassus">Crassus</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

